stream
From: =?ISO-8859-1?Q?J=F6rn_Kottmann?= <kottmann@gmail.com>
To: <users@opennlp.apache.org>
Reply-To: <users@opennlp.apache.org>
Subject: Re: Feature Generators
Date: Wed, 26 Feb 2014 08:50:04 +0100
Message-ID: <530D9CAC.5080901@gmail.com>
In-Reply-To: <CAJ+FrY6C_Hp_b-Pzx2VqUqnonx9Dei8kcXDV7j1wPT99mNKsuA@mail.gmail.com>
References: <CAJ+FrY6C_Hp_b-Pzx2VqUqnonx9Dei8kcXDV7j1wPT99mNKsuA@mail.gmail.com>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: multipart/alternative; boundary="=_Alt_eff67b56"

--=_Alt_eff67b56
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello,

the PreviousMapFeatureGenerator remebers the last outcome (Begin of 
name, Inside a name,
outside a name) for a token in all previous sentences. It shoud be 
cleared after the end of a document
with a call to the name finders clearAdaptivData method.

JÃ¶rn

On 02/25/2014 11:17 AM, Kenig Ma wrote:
> Hi,
>
> Is there documentation on the existing features generators? In particular I
> am looking at PreviousMapFeatureGenerator, trying to get my head around it
> but not sure if I understand what it is.
>
> Thanks
> Ken
>


--=_Alt_eff67b56
Content-Type: text/html; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

<div class="ea-plain-text" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Hello,

the PreviousMapFeatureGenerator remebers the last outcome (Begin of 
name, Inside a name,
outside a name) for a token in all previous sentences. It shoud be 
cleared after the end of a document
with a call to the name finders clearAdaptivData method.

JÃ¶rn

On 02/25/2014 11:17 AM, Kenig Ma wrote:
&gt; Hi,
&gt;
&gt; Is there documentation on the existing features generators? In particular I
&gt; am looking at PreviousMapFeatureGenerator, trying to get my head around it
&gt; but not sure if I understand what it is.
&gt;
&gt; Thanks
&gt; Ken
&gt;

</div>
--=_Alt_eff67b56--

endstream
endobj
